# GitRx document map

## November 6 continuation

The dated 209-file baseline below remains intact. New release work is summarized
in [the continuation report](../reports/continuation-20261106/REPORT.md),
[validation/adjudication](../reports/validation-v101-20261106/REPORT.md),
[section audit closure](../reports/section-schema-audit-20261103/REPORT.md),
and [schema/admission closure](../reports/schema-and-ingestion-20261103/REPORT.md).
New owner-facing entry points are [REPRODUCE](../REPRODUCE.md),
[SOURCES](../SOURCES.md), [SECURITY](../SECURITY.md), [MCP](../MCP.md),
[LIMITATIONS](../LIMITATIONS.md), and the [searchable coverage report](../reports/continuation-20261106/coverage.html).
The new [native browsing guide](NATIVE-BROWSING.md) documents source-first
queries over the expanded corpus without extending pilot context claims.
They supersede the earlier pending-recovery/undecided-policy status descriptions.

Consolidated November 5, 2026. This map accounts for **all 209 Markdown files present before this consolidation**, excluding `.git` and the virtual environment. It preserves them in place; it does not concatenate historical decisions into a misleading current specification.

## Read these first

1. [START-HERE.md](START-HERE.md): the project explained, with architecture, vocabulary, pipeline, queries and original-versus-built differences.
2. [BUILD-STATUS.md](BUILD-STATUS.md): current counts, completed work across three chats, unfinished audit, blockers and next steps.
3. This map: route from a topic or old stage name to its underlying evidence.

## How to resolve conflicting documents

Current behavior must be checked against its owning implementation and selected manifests. Accepted behavior contracts remain in [SPEC.md](../SPEC.md); apply later applicable overrides rather than the first status paragraph. Dated reports prove what was observed at their capture time. Current metadata establishes operational state. This consolidation summarizes those sources and explicitly labels uncertainty; it does not override accepted rules.

A document headed “latest,” “running,” “pending,” or “proposal only” may now be historical. In particular, the old HANDOFF and brief predate terminal acquisition, archive-route proposals predate admission, Block 1 stops predate the v1.0.1 repair, and the fresh validation design predates delivery of the current blank page. Frozen/candidate copies are reproducibility material. Do not update them merely to make their prose current.

